WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.950
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> ! Kyogoku- <i>san</i> !

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:16.450
It's been a month!

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.660
Come out of your room already!

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.370
Things were so nice back then...

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.330
That's right...

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.330
I'm sorry!

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:32.410
Why dun' we do it again?

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.200
"D-Dun"?

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.750
Ayup. Dat's right.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:38.370
Now...

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.950
Fuyuto Kyogoku is on his way!

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.250
I hast fallen!

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.000
He's just a physical and mental mess,

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:32.290
"Take Back Your Melon Heart"

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:30.870
and he needs to spend some time in the hospital.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.290
You listening?

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:35.160
Hey, so was Gokkun still alive?

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:37.000
Yeah. Just barely.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:40.950
Oh, I thought he was dead.

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:44.370
He's had a hard time.

00:02:44.370 --> 00:02:47.500
Let's go see him in the
hospital and cheer him up.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:54.000
John, Fuyuto's wounds are deeper
than the Mariana Trench.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.040
The love of his life was a serial killer.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.700
And is dead.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:00.620
And also was a man.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.330
There's no coming back from that.

00:03:08.830 --> 00:03:10.870
Heya general, how about a drink?

00:03:10.870 --> 00:03:13.370
Some other time...

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:15.750
Get lost.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.500
Afro.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:22.410
What's up, kid?

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:24.450
Afro.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:29.830
Legendary... detective...

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.410
Hey!

00:03:34.410 --> 00:03:39.540
Eat up, Futaro- <i>chan</i> !

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.540
"Patient at Melon Hospital"
 "Client"

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.830
I'm surprised you knew
about the row house, though.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:47.000
It's famous online and on 3.5 channel.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.790
Six legendary detectives
who lurk deep in Kabukicho.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.790
"Six legendary detectives
in the darkness of Kabukicho..."

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.870
"Terrifying Black Afro Guards the Gate"

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:53.870
Their gate guided by a terrifying black afro.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.160
And the owner is an ancient
hag monster with too much makeup!

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.580
How terrible!

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:02.120
So, what's the job?

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.580
Teleporting to another world!

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.450
Like you see in those online novels.

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.500
It happened in Shinjuku East
Melon Memorial Hospital.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:18.790
That's where Kyogoku- <i>san</i> is hospitalized.

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:26.120
Something very strange happened to me
and the other boy in my room, Ranpo- <i>kun</i> .

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.330
Like always, I was reading my books,

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.750
and Ranpo- <i>kun</i> went to sleep early.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.830
I went to sleep soon after, but...

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:42.200
...something felt weird, and I woke up and...

00:04:45.290 --> 00:04:49.160
...we were transported to another world!

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.200
When I woke up...

00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:12.290
...he was gone!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:16.160
I must've been sent back here alone,

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:20.500
while Ranpo- <i>kun</i> is still in the other world!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.330
But...

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:30.040
Um, Ranpo- <i>kun</i> left the hospital.
His mom came to get him.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:34.040
I know they're lying.

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:38.040
And the police won't do a thing.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:39.910
Don't you think that's weird?

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:42.370
Well, I think you're weird.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:43.910
You were dreaming, right?

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.580
It wasn't a dream.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:48.790
You believe me, right, mister?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:50.580
Miss.

00:05:50.580 --> 00:05:54.580
Isn't it possible he ran away
from the hospital, like you did?

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.830
Or it was a prank?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.290
Impossible.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:05:59.500
Ranpo- <i>kun</i> wasn't that type.

00:05:59.500 --> 00:06:05.910
When I invited him to leave the hospital
and go play, he never went with me.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:09.160
He's a very honest and good kid
who understands what it means

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.450
to be a son of Melon Hospital's director.

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.500
Please, detectives.

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:16.540
Bring Ranpo- <i>kun</i> back!

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:19.500
He's my friend!

00:06:19.500 --> 00:06:22.950
Did you bring anything to pay us with?

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.750
Of course.

00:06:25.750 --> 00:06:26.660
What are these?

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.750
Talismans to increase your magical power.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.040
They boost your MP by 100!

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.200
Okay, I'm out.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.200
They said on the internet that you'd
take payment in things other than money.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.330
Only Kobayashi would want that.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:41.950
Fine, bring him here then...

00:06:41.950 --> 00:06:45.410
He left to buy the new game console

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:48.200
and has been standing in line since last night.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.160
I'll take the job.

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:51.500
Really?

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:56.000
Hooray! Thank you!

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:56.000
That's right. There's one other guy here
who doesn't need money to work.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.330
Yeah.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:04.450
So, you're supposed
to be in the hospital, right?

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:06.250
Is it okay for you to be out of bed?

00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:10.250
It's fine. I almost never have the fits.

00:07:10.250 --> 00:07:12.290
No need to worry.

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:14.160
What's in there, by the way?

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:18.330
Well, you see, I know somebody else
who's hospitalized there.

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.160
I'm going to pay him a visit.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.410
There's no need to visit a guy like that.

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:25.200
Why don't we just stop in and say hi?

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:31.540
Hey, do you have a bag?

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:33.830
Yeah.

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:36.870
Go on without me.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:38.620
I'll catch up.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.910
Okay. Let's go, Futaro- <i>kun</i> .

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:43.000
Okay.

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:49.660
"Shinjuku East Melon 
Memorial Hospital"

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.000
What is that? A melon?

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.660
It's a planetarium that's under construction.

00:07:49.660 --> 00:07:52.950
It's going to be a symbol of the hospital.

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:56.370
Futaro- <i>kun</i> !

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:58.620
You can't keep running away from your room!

00:07:58.620 --> 00:08:00.000
Come over here!

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.620
Okay! Detective, take care of the rest!

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.410
No running!

00:08:07.410 --> 00:08:09.120
I'm fine!

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:13.870
I really appreciate this.

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:19.040
"Melon Hospital Director"

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:21.950
Trust means everything in this business.
So it's hard for me to go to the cops.

00:08:21.950 --> 00:08:23.500
Director Yokomizo,

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:29.120
does that mean your son,
Ranpo- <i>kun</i> , really vanished?

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.700
I searched the whole hospital...

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:35.540
Looks like this "other world"
is somewhere in the hospital.

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:38.370
Does that mean they've got
their own in-house dragon?

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.120
You're not as far off as you might think.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:47.000
Yokomizo- <i>san</i> , who first noticed
Ranpo- <i>kun</i> was missing?

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:50.830
Me. I'm Harukiyo Matsumoto, his secretary.

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:56.750
"Melon Hospital Secretary"

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:53.290
Matsumoto- <i>kun</i> here's been very
concerned about my son's health,

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:56.750
and has spent a lot of time
going to see him in his room.

00:08:56.750 --> 00:09:00.870
The nurse said his mom took him home...

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.830
That's what I've told the staff.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:06.500
I don't want an uproar...

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:10.750
My wife and I separated. He's not with her.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:16.790
We suspected a kidnapping, but
there've been no ransom demands...

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:21.370
Something seems up with that director.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:24.660
He seems way too calm...

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.370
Um...

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:33.700
Is Fuyuto Kyogoku doing well?

00:09:33.700 --> 00:09:37.290
I've known him since preschool.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:41.080
He's a patient here right now...

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.950
Both Fuyuto and I were very sickly as children.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:51.080
We spent a lot of time here.

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:54.250
Extreme!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:54.820
Ex!

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:55.370
Cali!

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.250
Bur!

00:09:57.250 --> 00:10:04.410
At the time there weren't a lot
of children here, so we became friends.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:08.250
It was always Fuyuto, me, and one more...

00:10:10.910 --> 00:10:13.450
I have fallen...

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:15.450
A boy named Ango.

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:17.660
"A Patient at Melon Hospital"

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:17.660
The three of us always played together.

00:10:17.660 --> 00:10:20.290
"Hospital School"

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:20.290
I'm gonna be a doctor!

00:10:20.290 --> 00:10:24.370
I want to be one, too, but I don't
have a dad, and my family's poor.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:26.700
You've never heard of student loans?

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.040
If you want to study, they'll lend you
the cash and you pay it back.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:32.250
Really? Then I'll study!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.500
What about you, Fuyuto?

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:35.870
I'm scared of blood...

00:10:35.870 --> 00:10:38.830
Then be one of the people who makes a hospital.

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:42.040
But you need a lot of money to do that...

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:44.790
So you'll need to go to the
West Side to make your fortune.

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.500
Make my fortune?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:49.950
Be a cool, rich guy.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:52.410
This book talks all about it.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:56.790
You make the hospital,
and Harukiyo and I will work there.

00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.410
We can cure all the adults and the kids,

00:10:58.410 --> 00:11:00.080
and the rich people and the poor people,

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:03.160
and the good people and the bad people, too.

00:11:03.160 --> 00:11:04.540
The bad people?

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:06.950
I don't want to help bad people.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:09.330
We'll help anybody who needs it.

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:12.040
That's what you do
if you're a cool doctor, right?

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:28.910
Hey, you brought a gift, right, Sherlock?

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.040
Yeah.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.500
Take it.

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:42.160
'Sup.

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:52.660
That disgusting pervert!

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:57.080
What art I doing?

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.910
Where art I be?

00:11:58.910 --> 00:12:00.830
A hospital in the East Side...

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:04.910
Thou...

00:12:04.910 --> 00:12:09.250
Is the way you're talking Extreme Excalibur?

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:12.910
Thou dost have a job for me?

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.200
You have the skills, right?

00:12:15.200 --> 00:12:19.160
But I art no longer a detective...

00:12:20.540 --> 00:12:26.290
That kid who vanished, Ranpo,
has the same disease Ango did.

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:30.620
Take it.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.080
"Western Dream"

00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:38.000
Why? I thought this was your treasure.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.790
I've memorized it all.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:55.700
I just can't help think of Ango
when I look at him.

00:12:57.910 --> 00:13:02.830
I need the help of a cool detective. Please.

00:13:07.370 --> 00:13:08.790
Fuyuto?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.410
I shalt head to investigate.

00:13:23.290 --> 00:13:27.500
Then there's someone here 24 hours a day?

00:13:27.500 --> 00:13:31.910
Yes. We checked all the
security camera footage, too,

00:13:31.910 --> 00:13:34.750
and didn't see anybody suspicious.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.910
I see.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:43.620
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> ! Are you okay?

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:45.130
I'm worried about your health...

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:46.300
Ignore me!

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:52.080
Matsumoto- <i>san</i> told me you're
going to help with the investigation?

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.220
I'll help you, so let's work together--

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.370
Silence!

00:13:58.410 --> 00:14:00.410
Hold me tighter!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:01.580
Okay!

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:04.080
So where are we going?

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.870
The scene of the crime.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.250
Understood.

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:10.660
Give it back, mister!

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:12.080
Hey!

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.040
Shut up!

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:16.040
Hey, I know the answer!

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.040
"You there!"

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.870
What? Come on, I got that one right!

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:19.870
What art that fool doing?

00:14:19.870 --> 00:14:23.120
It's the new game console.

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:25.580
Supposedly really realistic.

00:14:25.580 --> 00:14:27.700
Realistic...

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:32.040
Kobayashi stood outside
all night lined up for it.

00:14:33.580 --> 00:14:36.290
<i>All</i> ! <i>The</i> ! <i>Boobs</i> !

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:42.500
There should be a secret
passage to the other world...

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:46.910
That's right! That must be
how he was taken out of here!

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.830
Come on, that's ridiculous.

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:59.120
They're all letters from his mom.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:03.450
I guess she can't come to see him...

00:15:04.950 --> 00:15:07.410
There art none for this week.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.500
Huh? That's odd.

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:12.950
Matsumoto- <i>san</i> brings them every week.

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:14.540
I was sure he brought one this week...

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:18.200
Does that mean somebody took it?

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:23.000
It probably contained the code
to reach the last boss.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.330
I see!

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:25.910
Right, right.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.580
I hath solved the mystery.

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:37.290
What's going on here?

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:38.500
Ssh!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:54.080
Liar! You said you'd let me see Mommy!

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:55.830
That's Ranpo- <i>kun</i> 's voice.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.910
Harukiyo!

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.290
Yokomizo- <i>san</i> ?

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:06.540
What are you doing here?

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:10.500
I can explain! There's a really good reason-

00:16:10.500 --> 00:16:13.250
Well done.

00:16:13.250 --> 00:16:17.370
I didn't think you'd make it this far, Fuyuto.

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.790
What's going on here?

00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:24.950
Nothing unusual was found
at the scene of the disappearance.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.000
There were no witnesses.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:32.580
But everything makes sense if you
assume Ranpo- <i>kun</i> left on his own.

00:16:32.580 --> 00:16:36.040
Ranpo- <i>kun</i> ? Why?

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:39.200
Mommy told me to...

00:16:39.200 --> 00:16:41.870
She said I could see her if I did...

00:16:42.950 --> 00:16:46.700
Harukiyo most likely rewrote the letter.

00:16:49.410 --> 00:16:55.660
And Ranpo- <i>kun</i> fled the hospital
using the same route Futaro- <i>kun</i> did.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:58.910
Then the other world I saw?

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:01.290
That game system.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:06.660
Harukiyo ordered Ranpo- <i>kun</i> to put it on you.

00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:10.870
And then in the morning, Harukiyo removed it.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.870
So that was it...

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:15.370
But why go through the trouble?

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:18.000
Futaro- <i>kun</i> had a habit of escaping the hospital.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.290
It was likely that he would tell the police
of Ranpo- <i>kun</i> 's disappearance.

00:17:22.290 --> 00:17:25.540
But if what he said was that
he went to another world...

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:28.450
No one would take him seriously.

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:29.270
Come with me!

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:30.830
Wait, Ranpo!

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.580
Ranpo!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:33.790
Harukiyo!

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.290
Harukiyo, give up!

00:17:41.870 --> 00:17:43.120
Stop it!

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.750
Let go of Ranpo- <i>kun</i> !

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:47.750
You're not the kind of person
who would do something like this!

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:51.950
You and Ango swore to be doctors
who would save people, right?

00:17:51.950 --> 00:17:54.040
What do you know?

00:17:54.040 --> 00:17:57.000
I gave up on that a long time ago!

00:17:57.000 --> 00:18:01.500
You're no different. You're a detective
in some dump on the East Side, right?

00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:05.620
I haven't given up on my dreams yet.

00:18:05.620 --> 00:18:09.580
I wanted to at least work in medicine
even if I couldn't be a doctor.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:13.080
So I managed to get hired here.

00:18:13.080 --> 00:18:15.870
But here's where it gets funny.

00:18:17.830 --> 00:18:22.200
Yokomizo, the director, was my father.

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:25.910
He hired me out of sympathy
when he saw what a failure I was.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:33.410
At first I was grateful, but...

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:39.870
He wanted Ranpo to take over the hospital.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:45.290
He gave him the best education money could buy
to make him into a great doctor.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:49.950
Even though he barely gave
me and my mom a dime!

00:18:49.950 --> 00:18:53.830
So I decided to use Ranpo to blackmail him.

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:57.160
So I could inherit the hospital!

00:18:57.160 --> 00:18:59.160
You're disappointed, aren't you?

00:18:59.160 --> 00:19:03.450
I'm not who you thought I was.

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.500
Thou canst still start over.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:10.080
Let's start over together...

00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:15.250
Fuyuto, the reason I hired you

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.660
was that I thought a shitty
detective from a dump

00:19:17.660 --> 00:19:20.910
would just make a mess of the investigation.

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:22.450
That's horrible!

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:26.370
We'll help anybody who needs it.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.410
That's what you do
if you're a cool doctor, right?

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:34.370
That's so lame...

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:41.910
You and I are both so lame.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:45.540
Right, Harukiyo?

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:49.870
It's time for our last Extreme Excalibur.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:54.750
Let's go to hell together, Harukiyo...

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.370
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> !

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:02.750
Let the battle...

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.250
...begin!

00:20:16.160 --> 00:20:17.950
Not yet.

00:20:19.120 --> 00:20:23.290
We're not done for yet.

00:20:27.620 --> 00:20:29.540
Fuyuto...

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:35.950
Kyogoku- <i>san</i> , you're crazy...

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:43.330
How is a disappearing act
like an otherworld fantasy?

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:44.910
I don't know, how?

00:20:44.910 --> 00:20:48.370
It's a miracle if it has a satisfying ending.

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:53.410
Thanks, Sherlock.

00:20:53.410 --> 00:20:55.500
For what?

00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:57.870
For giving him hints to solve the case

00:20:57.870 --> 00:21:00.410
and helping cure him with the poop.

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:04.160
You tried to help him get better, right?

00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:09.000
Mr. Detective,

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.700
here's your talisman for a reward.

00:21:13.700 --> 00:21:15.870
I'll take it.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:22.040
When I grow up,
I'm going to be a detective, too!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.580
I must go.

00:21:27.580 --> 00:21:32.830
The case calls Fuyuto Kyogoku,
the cool guy detective.

00:21:38.660 --> 00:21:48.950
N-No one.... can... stop me...

00:21:48.950 --> 00:21:50.540
'Sup.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.000
"Tokyo 7th Prison"

00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:33.910
Hey, that was nice of you.

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:35.580
Thanks.

00:23:49.330 --> 00:23:50.870
What's wrong?

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:55.040
You're kidding...

00:23:55.040 --> 00:23:56.160
He's dead?

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:56.830
Guards!

00:23:56.830 --> 00:23:57.830
Get back!

00:23:57.830 --> 00:23:59.950
Get away from him!

00:23:59.950 --> 00:24:04.950
"Where is He?"

00:24:00.330 --> 00:24:04.950
This doesn't make sense! I'm so worried!

00:24:04.950 --> 00:24:06.910
"An Explanation of the Mysterious Character
That Appeared in the Episode"
"Only to hide animal poop.
Beneath the character is real poop."
